<div class="page-header">
  <h2>Getting Started</h2>
  <p class="page-desc">Follow these steps to set up Legacy GovCon and start tracking your first opportunity.</p>
</div>

<div class="gs-steps">

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">1</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Set up your company profile</h3>
      <p>Add your company name, address, UEI/DUNS number, and cage code. This information populates your capability statements and proposal cover sheets.</p>
      <a href="/settings#general" class="btn btn-primary">Go to Settings</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">2</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Review your NAICS codes</h3>
      <p>NAICS codes define what types of government contracts your business is eligible for. The system comes pre-loaded with common codes — mark the ones that apply to your work as primary.</p>
      <a href="/settings#naics" class="btn btn-primary">Review NAICS Codes</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">3</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Set your tracked keywords</h3>
      <p>Keywords are used to filter and score incoming opportunities by relevance. Add terms related to your services, industry, and target agencies.</p>
      <a href="/settings#keywords" class="btn btn-primary">Edit Keywords</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">4</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Add an institution</h3>
      <p>Institutions are the agencies, foundations, or organizations that issue the contracts and grants you pursue. Start with the agencies you work with most.</p>
      <a href="/institutions/new" class="btn btn-primary">Add Institution</a>
      <div class="gs-example">
        <strong>Examples:</strong> Department of Defense, HHS, City of Los Angeles, W.K. Kellogg Foundation
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">5</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Add key contacts</h3>
      <p>Contacts are the people at those institutions — contracting officers, program managers, grant officers, and technical points of contact.</p>
      <a href="/contacts/new" class="btn btn-primary">Add Contact</a>
      <div class="gs-example">
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Link contacts to their institution so you can see your full relationship map by agency.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">6</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Add your first opportunity</h3>
      <p>An opportunity is any contract, grant, job, or subcontract you're considering pursuing. Enter the basic details — title, type, due date, and estimated value — and set its status to <strong>Reviewing</strong> or <strong>Pursuing</strong>.</p>
      <a href="/opportunities/new" class="btn btn-primary">Add Opportunity</a>
      <div class="gs-example">
        <strong>Government contract?</strong> Use the <a href="/government/new">Government Contracts</a> form — it captures solicitation number, set-aside type, and NAICS code.<br>
        <strong>Grant?</strong> Use the <a href="/grants/new">Grant Opportunities</a> form — it tracks award range, eligibility, and funder details.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">7</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Move it to your pipeline</h3>
      <p>Once you decide to actively pursue an opportunity, add it to your pipeline. Open the opportunity's detail page and click <strong>"Add to Pipeline"</strong>. Assign a stage, win probability, and next action.</p>
      <div class="gs-pipeline-stages">
        <span class="badge">Identified</span>
        <span class="gs-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="badge">Qualified</span>
        <span class="gs-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="badge">Pursuing</span>
        <span class="gs-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="badge">Proposal In Progress</span>
        <span class="gs-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="badge">Submitted</span>
        <span class="gs-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="badge">Negotiating</span>
        <span class="gs-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="badge">Awarded</span>
      </div>
      <div class="gs-example">
        <strong>Terminal stages:</strong> a pipeline item ends at <strong>Awarded</strong>, or at <strong>Lost</strong> or <strong>Withdrawn</strong> if it doesn't go your way — both are also valid stops from any point in the sequence.
      </div>
      <div class="gs-example">
        <strong>Note:</strong> Pipeline Stage and the opportunity's own <strong>Status</strong> field are intentionally separate and don't update each other — see the note on the Pipeline page for why.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step">
    <div class="gs-step-num">8</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Track and update as you work</h3>
      <p>As the bid progresses, update the pipeline stage and log next actions. When an opportunity is won, set its Status and pipeline Stage to <strong>Awarded</strong>, then manually create a <strong>Project</strong> (Projects → + Add) and an <strong>Award History</strong> entry (Award History → + Add) to record it — winning an opportunity does not automatically create these; that's a deliberate manual step so you control what gets recorded as past performance.</p>
      <a href="/pipeline" class="btn btn-primary">View Pipeline</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="gs-step gs-step--resources">
    <div class="gs-step-num">&#9670;</div>
    <div class="gs-step-body">
      <h3>Additional resources</h3>
      <div class="gs-resource-grid">
        <div class="gs-resource">
          <strong>Bid Writing Guides</strong>
          <p>Store your proposal templates, past performance narratives, and win themes here so they're ready when you need them fast.</p>
          <a href="/guides" class="btn-link">Go to Guides →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="gs-resource">
          <strong>Award History</strong>
          <p>Log every bid outcome — win or lose. Over time this becomes your past performance record and helps sharpen your bid/no-bid decisions.</p>
          <a href="/award-history" class="btn-link">Go to Award History →</a>
        </div>
        <div class="gs-resource">
          <strong>Funders</strong>
          <p>If you pursue grants, track the foundations and agencies that fund your area of work — giving cycles, priorities, and relationship notes.</p>
          <a href="/funders" class="btn-link">Go to Funders →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
